  <content>
    <procedure>
      <commonInfo><title>Job description</title><para>This procedure gives the functional test of the actuator.</para></commonInfo>
      <preliminaryRqmts><reqCondGroup><noConds/></reqCondGroup><reqPersons><personnel numRequired="1"><personCategory personCategoryCode="Shop technician"/><personSkill skillLevelCode="sk02"/><estimatedTime unitOfMeasure="h">0.5</estimatedTime></personnel></reqPersons><reqSupportEquips><supportEquipDescrGroup><supportEquipDescr id="seq-adt-7100-02"><name>Holding fixture, rod end</name><identNumber><manufacturerCode>ZZD01</manufacturerCode><partAndSerialNumber><partNumber>ADT-7100-02</partNumber></partAndSerialNumber></identNumber><reqQuantity unitOfMeasure="EA">1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr><supportEquipDescr id="seq-fg-0500"><name>Force gauge, 0 to 500 N</name><toolRef toolNumber="FG-0500"/><reqQuantity unitOfMeasure="EA">1</reqQuantity></supportEquipDescr></supportEquipDescrGroup></reqSupportEquips><reqSupplies><noSupplies/></reqSupplies><reqSpares><noSpares/></reqSpares><reqSafety><noSafety/></reqSafety></preliminaryRqmts>
      <mainProcedure><proceduralStep><para>Install the actuator in the holding fixture, <internalRef internalRefId="seq-adt-7100-02" internalRefTargetType="irtt05"/>.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Pull the release lever (70) with the force gauge, <internalRef internalRefId="seq-fg-0500" internalRefTargetType="irtt05"/>. The lock must release at 20 to 30 N (4.5 to 6.7 lbf).</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>With the lever released, apply a compressive load of 1000 N (225 lbf) to the rod end (30). The piston rod must not move.</para></proceduralStep><proceduralStep><para>Measure the full stroke. It must be 74 to 76 mm (2.91 to 2.99 in).</para><note><notePara>If the actuator does not pass this test, disassemble it (<dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="ASTDEMO" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="25" subSystemCode="2" subSubSystemCode="1" assyCode="71" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="530" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="C"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>) and examine the parts against the fits and clearances (<dmRef><dmRefIdent><dmCode modelIdentCode="ASTDEMO" systemDiffCode="A" systemCode="25" subSystemCode="2" subSubSystemCode="1" assyCode="71" disassyCode="00" disassyCodeVariant="A" infoCode="030" infoCodeVariant="A" itemLocationCode="C"/></dmRefIdent></dmRef>).</notePara></note></proceduralStep></mainProcedure>
      <closeRqmts><reqCondGroup><noConds/></reqCondGroup></closeRqmts>
    </procedure>
